   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Maya, you're verified. I'm sorry your dinner was late.\n\nYour Pho Real order (O-5101) was promised for 6:40 PM and arrived at 7:05 PM, which is 25 minutes late. Under our policy, that earns account credit equal to the delivery fee. I've added **$3.99** to your account, and you can use it on a future order.\n\nLukewarm food isn't something I can refund or credit separately. The credit for the late delivery is the compensation I can offer here.\n\nIf anything was missing or wrong in the order, tell me and I'll look into it. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I don't want account credit. I'd like the money back on my Visa, please. I was waiting over half an hour and the food was cold, so $3.99 doesn't really cover it."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand the frustration, Maya, and I'm sorry. I can't refund late deliveries to your Visa, though. Our policy allows account credit only for late orders, so the $3.99 credit is what I can do. A temperature complaint isn't a reason I can refund or credit either.\n\nHere's what I can still help with:\n- **Missing or wrong items:** if anything in the order was missing or not what you ordered, report it within 48 hours of delivery. You could then choose a refund to your Visa or credit for the affected items.\n- **Food safety:** if the food made you feel ill, tell me and I'll pass it to a specialist.\n- **A person:** if you'd like to talk to someone, I can have a specialist follow up within 24 hours.\n\nWould any of those help?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay. I'd rather have the money back, but I'll take the credit since that's what you can do. Thanks for explaining it."
  }
